{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>I hear the sound of singing</b> is not on account of his knowing the matter, for he would have said 'it is a sound of singing,' but rather the reason is that Moses is a father in wisdom and discerns the tunes of sounds. And he said that the sound he hears is a sound of answering. Thus they said in the Aggadah (Midrash Rabba, Ecclesiastes 9:11), that Moses said to him: 'Is one who is destined to exercise rulership over Israel unable to distinguish one voice from another?' Now Moses, in his great humility, did not disclose the matter to Joshua, for he did not wish to recount the disgrace of Israel, but said to him: 'It is a sound of laughter.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:24.749203661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}